  {
   "id": "e_35",
   "pageId": "p_02",
   "sectionId": "s_32",
   "type": "text",
   "name": "Description",
   "content": {
    "text": "The house sits low between rows of apple trees, so that from the lane you see the orchard first and the house second. A brick ground floor holds the kitchen and living rooms; a lighter timber-framed floor above holds the bedrooms and looks out over the trees.\n\nThe brick was made a few miles away. Inside, the floors are oak and the stair is a single plaster curve with oak treads, lit from a roof light.",
    "fontFamily": "Inter",
    "fontSize": 16,
    "fontWeight": 400,
    "align": "left",
    "sample": true
   },
   "sortOrder": 2
  },
